<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ib8daa70775ced0c14e3210f0491245749bae6973" commit="b38f328476b6d6024164afb0d146205b9e3b12ad" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/nouveau: Add delta to nvkm_vm_get_*()  Add delta to nvkm_vm_get() and nvkm_vm_get_offset().  We then set the delta and length of the vma to track the exact (sub)region of the buffer that this vma will represent.  This is to support the partial mapping/unmapping of a buffer.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49979 TEST=Build and boot to desktop on A44  Change-Id: Ib8daa70775ced0c14e3210f0491245749bae6973 Signed-off-by: Andrew Chew &lt;achew@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329875 Reviewed-by: Vince Hsu &lt;vince.h@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329875" owner_email="achew@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/75/329875/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ifa02d4c893159572c8c6c268fd9dcb7c6cf8479f" commit="4a941e0dab4cd146c243a6756dbbd979a473b4f4" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/nouveau: Move delta large page alignment WARN_ON  Move the WARN_ON to a condition where it's specifically relevant, because gk20a_instobj_map_sg() can be entered in the small page case as well, where this WARN_ON wouldn't be valid.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49979 TEST=Build and boot to desktop on A44  Change-Id: Ifa02d4c893159572c8c6c268fd9dcb7c6cf8479f Signed-off-by: Andrew Chew &lt;achew@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329876 Reviewed-by: Vince Hsu &lt;vince.h@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329876" owner_email="achew@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/76/329876/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I990a470292187319225f8acd33553f9264ec95f3" commit="44be59f55f81c98b1e7beb2d8d48d80e001d7805" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/nouveau: Fix nvkm_vm_map_*() for delta  Fix nvkm_vm_map_*() calls to honor the delta parameter for purposes of starting a mapping offset from the start by delta bytes.  This is to support partial mapping/unmapping of a buffer.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49979 TEST=Build and boot to desktop on A44  Change-Id: I990a470292187319225f8acd33553f9264ec95f3 Signed-off-by: Andrew Chew &lt;achew@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329877 Reviewed-by: Vince Hsu &lt;vince.h@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329877" owner_email="achew@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/77/329877/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ib4dc3162b680f42035abdef640eff3b7e3ba877f" commit="dd3b6ff2a4899afd6bf509708e99dfaa2883b0ad" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/nouveau: For iommu mapping, map size of mem  Rather than mapping the region described by the nvkm_vma, map the region described by nvkm_mem.  In the case of partial mapping, we may have many nvkm_vma's that describe subregions of the nvkm_mem.  However, we want to map the entire nvkm_mem region once to the iommu.  When nvkm_vm_map_sg_table_with_iommu() is entered again with a different subregion nvkm_vma, we will seemingly redo the iommu mapping for the same nvkm_mem region...however, this iommu mapping is refcounted, so we won't do the iommu mapping again redundantly.  In fact, we rely on this refcounting so that when we eventually call mmu-&gt;unmap_iommu(), these unmaps get ref-uncounted properly and the iommu mapping undone only once at the last nvkm_vma unmapping.  In the more normal case of the nvkm_vma spanning exactly the region described by the nvkm_mem, there is no change in behavior.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49979 TEST=Build and boot to desktop on A44  Change-Id: Ib4dc3162b680f42035abdef640eff3b7e3ba877f Signed-off-by: Andrew Chew &lt;achew@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329878 Reviewed-by: Vince Hsu &lt;vince.h@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329878" owner_email="achew@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/78/329878/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I462c1ecbff0f784cf9369178cc99a1f820661a5b" commit="f4909c6432914e20d43a3a222f726454dc10bf97" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/nouveau: Add nouveau_bo_subvma_*() functions  Add functions for dealing with &quot;subvmas&quot; (which are vma's that span only part of a buffer).  This is for supporting partial mappings.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49979 TEST=Build and boot to desktop on A44  Change-Id: I462c1ecbff0f784cf9369178cc99a1f820661a5b Signed-off-by: Andrew Chew &lt;achew@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329879 Reviewed-by: Vince Hsu &lt;vince.h@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329879" owner_email="achew@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/79/329879/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Id82bdb6c3f31aaac2ff28cfcf7cee1774a6bd783" commit="cc